  "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{A}={\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{13}}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{B}={\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11}},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cap B}?$",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cap B}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{B}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{\u2015}{A}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{B} \\\\  & ={\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{13}}\\cup {\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11}} \\\\  & ={\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{11},\\sqrt{13}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
